{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788190214,"nonce":"uRnZ5U4dNm8Q4qjefDZ3n+6nmnY=","message":"CLOSED — verified live on the bench, merged fast-forward to main.\n\nTHE BULLET, driven twice with different raids\n\n- 400 points, 6 hostiles (3 grenadiers + 3 town guards): all six killed.\n- 700 points, 10 hostiles (waster/pirate/scavenger gunners, mercenaries): fought\n  and driven off.\n\nJournal `action` rows across the second fight:\n`{wear:11, equip:6, unforbid:2, assign:4, seek-at-will:5, drop:1, policy-new:1}`\n— **zero `draft`, zero `attack`, zero `move-to`.** Combat was fought entirely on\nthe toggle. That is the whole claim and it holds.\n\nALSO VERIFIED\n\n- Auto stance by weapon and skill: a Brawler with a plasma sword -\u003e close; three\n  Shooting-14 riflemen -\u003e far (0.9 of range), each echoing its own reasoning.\n- `on:\"auto\"` correctly turned an unarmed Melee-1 pawn OFF (\"seeking would make\n  this pawn a casualty\") and turned it back ON once armed.\n- The `drafted` gate refuses with the reason that says to undraft first.\n- `already` rejections write NO journal row.\n- The hostility warning fires on a REPEAT call — the regression the review\n  caught, confirmed fixed on the bench: warnings went 0 -\u003e 1 where it had been\n  silently 0.\n- Zero red errors across every run.\n\nTHE REVIEW WAS WORTH MORE THAN THE FIRST DRAFT. Nine confirmed defects before\nthis shipped, three of which defeated the verb's own purpose (the hostility\nwarning skipped on the common path; every read printing \"NOT WRITTEN — the\njournal writer is closed\"; every rejection discarding its diagnostics). All\nfixed and re-verified live. Detail is in the commit message on d5811f3.\n\nWHAT PLAY EXPOSED, filed separately, none of it seek-at-will's fault\n\n- `4087644` — job-ordering verbs report success for orders that did nothing.\n  Seen live during this very acceptance: `equip` returned `accepted:1` with\n  `job_def:\"Wait_MaintainPosture\"`.\n- `1a072fa` — no verb can turn on FSWA auto-arming, so pawns cannot arm\n  themselves.\n- `826d4bf` — no verb can use a targetable item (resurrector serum) on a target.\n\nPLAY LESSONS worth carrying into 4.1\n\n- Weapons dropped by downed or dead pawns are auto-forbidden by vanilla; 8 of 23\n  weapons on the map were unusable until `unforbid`. But do NOT unforbid during\n  a fight — a colonist immediately went to haul an assault rifle to a stockpile\n  mid-raid instead of shooting.\n- `equip` and `wear` are JOBS: the pawn must walk to the item. Combat interrupts\n  them. Arm before the fight, not during it — our best melee fighter spent an\n  engagement standing empty-handed because his equip never completed.\n- Seek releases a pawn when danger drops, even with hostiles still on the map: a\n  full-health swordsman went back to hauling wood with three raiders alive.","files":null}]}